REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,044621,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/fkfd-ctqq
           (J,PL/B,868,139713,2025)
           #doi:10.1016/j.physletb.2025.139713
            Same data given
FACILITY   (SYNCY,2ZZZCER)
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) CERN nTOF EAR1 experimental area
INC-SPECT  Neutron flux determined by a dedicated measurements
            using PPAC relying on 235U(n,f)
SAMPLE     Natural Carbon (5 cm x 5 cm, 0.25 mm thickness)
            mounted in vacuum chamber at 45 deg relative to the
            beam direction
METHOD     (TOF) Flight path of 182.5 m
           (EDE)
REL-REF    (M,,P.Zugec+,J,NIM/A,1033,166686,2022)
           Particle identification in (En,dE,E) space based on
            neural network
           (M,,P.Zugec+,J,JINS,15,P02011,2020)
           Data reduction procedure
           (M,,P.Zugec,J,NIM/A,983,164606,2020)
           Synchronization of signals from separate Si strips
DETECTOR   (TELES,SI,SI) Two telescopes made of two position
            sensitive dE (20 um) and E (300 um) Si detectors
CORRECTION Corrected for 12,13C(n,p)12,13B, 12,13C(n,d)11,12B
            angular distribution for various branches of boron
            excitation levels by adopting TALYS-2.0 simulation
            with 384 combinations of models and their parameters
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S)   Statistical uncertainty
           (ERR-1)   Uncertainty related to TALYS modelling
           (ERR-2)   Uncertainty related to flux (3%)
           (ERR-SYS) Total systematic uncertainty (ERR-1 & ERR-2)
           (ERR-T)   Total uncertainty (ERR-S & ERR-SYS)
